{"id":"f099bf27843654d6","group":"58","path":"58/batch06/58-df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining.md","title":"ZFC Measure8 Relatively Independent Joining","display":"df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining — ZFC Measure8 Relatively Independent Joining","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining","aliases":["58-df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining"],"display":"df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining — ZFC Measure8 Relatively Independent Joining","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-joining]]","[[58-df-product]]","[[../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md]]","[[../batch19/58-df-zfc-prob-probability-space.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-zfc-measure8-factor-map.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure8-conditional-independence.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-measure8-relatively-independent-joining — ZFC Measure8 Relatively Independent Joining"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4a3373ca17fc93e6\" href=\"?note=4a3373ca17fc93e6\" title=\"58-df-joining\">58-df-joining</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"3579e07be41aa5cd\" href=\"?note=3579e07be41aa5cd\" title=\"58-df-product\">58-df-product</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"a8bb827e3e31f34f\" href=\"?note=a8bb827e3e31f34f\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d4d304b0bbb11c1a\" href=\"?note=d4d304b0bbb11c1a\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-zfc-prob-probability-space.md\">../batch19/58-df-zfc-prob-probability-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"93f2d1f40aee7116\" href=\"?note=93f2d1f40aee7116\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-zfc-measure8-factor-map.md\">../batch17/58-df-zfc-measure8-factor-map.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"6be89bf537c52975\" href=\"?note=6be89bf537c52975\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure8-conditional-independence.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure8-conditional-independence.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu,T)\">\\((X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu,T)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu,S)\">\\((Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu,S)\\)</span> (probability-preserving systems)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C})\">\\((Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C})\\)</span> (a common probability-space factor)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q_X:X\\to Z\">\\(q_X:X\\to Z\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q_Y:Y\\to Z\">\\(q_Y:Y\\to Z\\)</span> (common-factor maps)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> (a joining measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\times Y\">\\(X\\times Y\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Joining}\">\\(\\mathrm{Joining}\\)</span> (joining predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"4a3373ca17fc93e6\" href=\"?note=4a3373ca17fc93e6\" title=\"58-df-joining\">58-df-joining</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3ProductSigmaAlgebra}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3ProductSigmaAlgebra}_S\\)</span> (product-sigma-algebra predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"a8bb827e3e31f34f\" href=\"?note=a8bb827e3e31f34f\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S\\)</span> (probability-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"d4d304b0bbb11c1a\" href=\"?note=d4d304b0bbb11c1a\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-zfc-prob-probability-space.md\">../batch19/58-df-zfc-prob-probability-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8FactorMap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8FactorMap}_S\\)</span> (factor-map predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"93f2d1f40aee7116\" href=\"?note=93f2d1f40aee7116\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-zfc-measure8-factor-map.md\">../batch17/58-df-zfc-measure8-factor-map.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConditionalIndependence}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConditionalIndependence}_S\\)</span> (conditional-independence predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"6be89bf537c52975\" href=\"?note=6be89bf537c52975\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure8-conditional-independence.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure8-conditional-independence.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8RelativelyIndependentJoining}_S\\subseteq V^{14}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8RelativelyIndependentJoining}_S\\subseteq V^{14}\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure8\\text{-}relatively\\text{-}independent\\text{-}joining}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8RelativelyIndependentJoining}_S(\n\\lambda,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C},T,S,X,Y,Z,\n\\mathcal B_X,\\mathcal B_Y,\\mu,\\nu,\\mathcal C,q_X,q_Y)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S(X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S(Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S(Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Joining}\\bigl(\\lambda;(X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu,T),(Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu,S)\\bigr)\n\\land\\exists R,\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y},\\mathcal A_X,\\mathcal A_Y,\\mathcal C_*\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3ProductSigmaAlgebra}_S(X,\\mathcal B_X,Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8FactorMap}_S(\nq_X,X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu,T,Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C},R)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8FactorMap}_S(\nq_Y,Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu,S,Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C},R)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathcal A_X=\\{A\\times Y:A\\in\\mathcal B_X\\}\n\\land\\mathcal A_Y=\\{X\\times B:B\\in\\mathcal B_Y\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathcal C_*=\n\\bigl\\{\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in X\\times Y:q_X(x)\\in C\\}:C\\in\\mathcal C\\bigr\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\forall C\\in\\mathcal C\\;\n\\lambda\\Bigl(\n\\bigl(q_X^{-1}[C]\\times Y\\bigr)\n\\mathbin\\triangle\n\\bigl(X\\times q_Y^{-1}[C]\\bigr)\\Bigr)=0\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConditionalIndependence}_S(\nX\\times Y,\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y},\\lambda,\n\\mathcal A_X,\\mathcal A_Y,\\mathcal C_*)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure8\\text{-}relatively\\text{-}independent\\text{-}joining}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8RelativelyIndependentJoining}_S(\n\\lambda,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C},T,S,X,Y,Z,\n\\mathcal B_X,\\mathcal B_Y,\\mu,\\nu,\\mathcal C,q_X,q_Y)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S(X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S(Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcProbProbabilitySpace}_S(Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Joining}\\bigl(\\lambda;(X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu,T),(Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu,S)\\bigr)\n\\land\\exists R,\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y},\\mathcal A_X,\\mathcal A_Y,\\mathcal C_*\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3ProductSigmaAlgebra}_S(X,\\mathcal B_X,Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8FactorMap}_S(\nq_X,X,\\mathcal B_X,\\mu,T,Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C},R)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8FactorMap}_S(\nq_Y,Y,\\mathcal B_Y,\\nu,S,Z,\\mathcal C,\\lambda_{\\mathcal C},R)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathcal A_X=\\{A\\times Y:A\\in\\mathcal B_X\\}\n\\land\\mathcal A_Y=\\{X\\times B:B\\in\\mathcal B_Y\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathcal C_*=\n\\bigl\\{\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in X\\times Y:q_X(x)\\in C\\}:C\\in\\mathcal C\\bigr\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\forall C\\in\\mathcal C\\;\n\\lambda\\Bigl(\n\\bigl(q_X^{-1}[C]\\times Y\\bigr)\n\\mathbin\\triangle\n\\bigl(X\\times q_Y^{-1}[C]\\bigr)\\Bigr)=0\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{15mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConditionalIndependence}_S(\nX\\times Y,\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y},\\lambda,\n\\mathcal A_X,\\mathcal A_Y,\\mathcal C_*)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span> is existentially quantified so the historical fourteen-argument interface is preserved while <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q_X\">\\(q_X\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q_Y\">\\(q_Y\\)</span> are required to be factor maps to one common dynamical system.</li>\n<li>The full joining signature fixes the given marginal systems, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y}\">\\(\\mathcal B_{X\\times Y}\\)</span> is an explicit witness for their product sigma-algebra.</li>\n<li>The symmetric-difference clause identifies the two pullbacks of every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C\\in\\mathcal C\">\\(C\\in\\mathcal C\\)</span> modulo <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span>; unlike a bare diagonal-support formula, it remains typed for arbitrary measurable factor spaces.</li>\n<li>Relative independence is ordinary conditional independence of the two coordinate sigma-algebras given that common pullback sigma-algebra. This avoids multiplying conditional-expectation representatives that live on different underlying spaces.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-joining","status":"resolved","id":"4a3373ca17fc93e6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-joining]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-product","status":"resolved","id":"3579e07be41aa5cd","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-product]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md","status":"resolved","id":"a8bb827e3e31f34f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-zfc-measure3-product-sigma-algebra.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-zfc-prob-probability-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"d4d304b0bbb11c1a","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../ba